WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.840
Good morning Hank, it's Sunday; it's news day. Today we're gonna talk about superstitious generals, Mormons, long-distance swimming, and the Nobel Peace Prize.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.420
Can ya guess the country to which I am referring?

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.584
Can ya? CAN YA?

00:00:09.584 --> 00:00:11.840
I'll give you the entire intro to come up with your answer.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.600
That's right, Hank, Burma!

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.360
Okay, Hank, first, a quick background of Burmese history, including a justification of why I am saying Burma and not Myanmar.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.120
Burma is a nation in Southeast Asia, bordering Thailand, China, and India.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:34.700
Burma was a British colony that gained its independence in 1948, and then from 1948 to 1962, had a kind of British-style democracy.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.800
And it was the wealthiest nation in Southeast Asia.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.940
And then in 1962, there was a military coup, and Burma got overtaken by crazy people.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:46.500
Hank, have you ever noticed that what happens after the words, "There was a military coup.", is generally pretty bad?

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:54.040
I wonder if there's any way we could get a memo out to, you know, like, militaries, explaining to them that, uh... 'coup-ing' is bad.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:59.080
So now, after 47 years of military rule, Burma is one of the poorest and most oppressive places in the world.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:04.860
Okay, so in 1989, the crazy military rulers of Burma decided that they were going to rename the country Myanmar.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.460
And now, lots of people refer to it as Myanmar. But I don't.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.000
Because if there was a military coup in the United States of America,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:18.000
and our new military rulers announced that the new name of our country was going to be the Democratic Socialist Republic of Poopyface Funnypants,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.800
I wouldn't want other people to call my homeland Poopyface Funnypants.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.400
So anyway, that's why I call it Burma.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.460
So, the original crazy Burmese general was a guy named Ne Win.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.680
Who bathed in the blood of dolphins, because he thought it would keep him young.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:35.620
And who famously tried to change the Burmese currency from base 10, like all other currencies in the world, to base 9,

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.560
because 9 was his lucky number.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.220
So for a while, all the currency in Burma was issued in multiples of nine.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:48.760
When it finally came time for Ne Win to resign, he decided to do it on the astrologically auspicious date of 8/8/88.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.680
Immediately after Ne Win resigned in 1988, there were these huge student protests.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.840
To which the Burmese government responded by killing more than 10 000 protesters.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.580
One of the leaders of these protests was a made-of-awesome woman named Aung San Suu Kyi.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:07.540
And in 1990, when the military government of Burma finally bowed to international pressure and agreed to have elections, Aung San Suu Kyi won!

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:11.760
And everyone was like: "This is great! We're gonna have this awesome lady as our prime minister!"

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:19.140
But the military was like: "No, nnnno. We said we would have elections. We didn't say that we would honour the results of those elections."

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:25.440
So Hank, the next year, Aung San Suu Kyi won the Nobel Peace Prize. And I'm sure you know what the Burmese government gives you if you win the Nobel Peace Prize.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.580
House arrest.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:31.560
In fact, Hank, Aung San Suu Kyi has been stuck inside of her lake-front house for most of the last twenty years.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:36.040
Aung San Suu Kyi is seen by the Burmese people in much the same way that Gandhi is seen by the Indian people.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.180
She's so popular that the Burmese generals are scared of killing her.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.860
But, Hank, a condition of her house arrest is that she's not allowed to have foreign visitors.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.020
Enter mentally disturbed Mormon evangelist American John Yettaw.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.020
Okay, Hank, so earlier this year, an American named John Yettaw abandoned his family and flew to Burma.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:54.620
He then swims across the large lake outside of Aung San Suu Kyi's house,

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.313
and shows up at her doorstep.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:03.160
Apparently, he was almost dead from the swim, so Aung San Suu Kyi, being the compassionate person she is, let him stay for a couple of days and recover.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.520
Then he got caught when he was trying to sneak back out.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:10.880
And now Aung San Suu Kyi has been arrested and faces 5 years in prison for violating the terms of her house arrest.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.340
So you get arrested and you go to prison because somebody swam to your house?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.800
How can the government get away with that, Hank?

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.800
One of the answers is that Burma's neighbours refuse to tell them, "Hey Burma! Stop being so crazy!"

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.200
Now obviously, it's hard to get a country like China fired up about human rights.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:31.440
But Burma's other neighbours, specifically India, need to put much more pressure on the Burmese government to really reform.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.340
Otherwise Burma will never have the opportunity to be led by its Gandhi.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:40.240
Hank, you'll see me on Tuesday, when Nerdfighters, I will be answering your questions. Please leave them in comments.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:45.520
By the way, Australian Nerdfighters, if you wanna see me in Sydney on June 3rd, there's information in the sidebar about how to book your spot.

